 const qs=[
 ['Visual purpose','A manager needs the exact invoice amount for one customer. Which choice best matches this task?',['A readable table with the exact amount','A decorative 3D pie','An unlabelled heat map','A word cloud'],0,'Exact-value retrieval often suits a table. Choose the representation against the question, rather than assuming a chart is always better.'],
 ['UX and tools','Which feature most directly supports dashboard customisation?',['A larger logo','A region filter with a visible selected state','An unexplained colour gradient','A permanently hidden denominator'],1,'A filter lets users choose a relevant subset; showing its state preserves context.'],
 ['UX and tools','Which is an observable UX evaluation criterion?',['It feels modern','It uses the most charts','A manager identifies the highest late rate correctly within 30 seconds','It is colourful'],2,'This connects a representative task to accuracy and completion time, making the judgement testable.'],
 ['Visual purpose','Which display best investigates the relationship between advertising spend and sales, with one pair per month?',['Pie chart','Network of staff','Histogram of store names','Scatter plot'],3,'A scatter plot preserves the paired numeric observations. Association does not establish causation.'],
 ['Security and storage','Which control most directly limits a logged-in manager to their own branch records?',['Role-based authorisation','A backup drive','A larger storage quota','A chart legend'],0,'Authentication checks identity. Authorisation controls what an authenticated identity can view or change.'],
 ['Visual purpose','Which representation best shows links between customer accounts in a referral network?',['Line chart of account IDs','Network diagram','Pie chart of login dates','Histogram of names'],1,'Nodes represent accounts and links represent relationships. This matches a connection question.'],
 ['Errors and bias','A designer publishes only months with positive profit. Which issue is most directly illustrated?',['Random sampling variation','A required form field','Selective reporting bias','Secure storage'],2,'Choosing only favourable results can systematically misrepresent the relevant full period.'],
 ['Blockchain','Which claim about blockchain is most defensible?',['It proves every physical input is true','Every blockchain is public','It removes all need for governance','It can make changes to a shared recorded history difficult to conceal'],3,'A tamper-evident ledger can support integrity. It does not prove the truth of an incorrectly recorded real-world event.'],
 ['Privacy and governance','A consent checkbox is present. What else must be considered before relying on consent?',['Whether the choice is informed, voluntary, current, specific and made with capacity','Only its colour','Whether it is preselected','Whether the text is long'],0,'A checkbox is a mechanism for recording a choice. It does not by itself establish meaningful consent.'],
 ['Big data and OLAP','Which statement illustrates variety most directly?',['A table grows from one to ten million identical-format rows','A dataset combines purchase tables, free-text reviews and images','A sensor sends a reading every second','A report loads in five seconds'],1,'Variety concerns different forms and structures. Volume is amount; velocity is arrival or processing rate.'],
 ['Big data and OLAP','A business cannot retain five years of records. Which requirement is most directly unmet?',['More decorative charts','Larger touch targets','Sufficient storage capacity','A new chart colour'],2,'Storage retains records for later use. Processing power alone does not provide retention capacity.'],
 ['Prediction and mining','Which activity best describes data mining?',['Storing a backup','Encrypting a login','Changing a page font','Exploring records to find useful recurring relationships'],3,'Mining looks for patterns and relationships. Storage, security and presentation support different parts of the workflow.'],
 ['Prediction and mining','A model is evaluated on the same examples used to fit it. What is the main concern?',['The result may overstate performance on genuinely new cases','The examples become automatically anonymous','The model must be perfectly accurate','All test errors must be zero'],0,'A model may fit its training examples while generalising poorly. Use appropriate unseen evaluation data.'],
 ['Security and storage','Why is a warehouse not an alternative location category to cloud storage in every comparison?',['Warehouses cannot store data','A warehouse can itself be hosted in the cloud','Cloud systems never support analysis','Local systems are always offline'],1,'Warehouse describes an analytical role/architecture, while cloud describes a hosting/service arrangement. These can overlap.'],
 ['Privacy and governance','Which item is metadata?',['The total monthly revenue','A customer purchase','The dataset collection date, units and field definitions','The result of SUM alone'],2,'Metadata describes the dataset and its context, helping users judge meaning, suitability and provenance.'],
 ['Privacy and governance','Which pairing is correct in the Australian federal privacy framework?',['OAIC is a spreadsheet function','APPs are a cloud storage brand','The Privacy Act is a data-cleaning tool','OAIC is the regulator and APPs are principles applying to covered entities'],3,'Distinguish the law, its principles and the regulator. Scope and exceptions matter.'],
 ['Social behaviour','A recommendation feed repeatedly reinforces the views a user already holds. Which concern is most relevant?',['An echo chamber','A mandatory zero baseline','A foreign-key error','An absolute reference'],0,'Repeatedly selected similar perspectives can limit exposure to alternatives and reinforce existing beliefs.'],
 ['Big data and OLAP','Which is a dimension in “sum of revenue by product and region”?',['Revenue','Region','The sum itself','The currency symbol'],1,'Region and product organise the numeric measure. Revenue is the measure being summarised.'],
 ['Big data and OLAP','Which action is refinement rather than performance optimisation?',['Caching a validated summary','Improving query execution','Reconciling duplicate product IDs using a documented mapping','Adding an index to support retrieval'],2,'Refinement improves suitability/quality. Optimisation improves the efficiency of storage, processing or retrieval.'],
 ['Big data and OLAP','How can a dashboard keep detail available without drawing every transaction at once?',['Hide the source permanently','Use more 3D charts','Remove every unusual value','Show summaries with filters and drill-down detail'],3,'Progressive detail balances an understandable overview with access to specific evidence.'],
 ['Errors and bias','Two bars show 92 and 96 purchases but begin at 90. What is the main concern?',['Displayed lengths of 2 and 6 exaggerate the relative difference','The real difference becomes 6','South actually has three times the purchases','Starting at 90 changes the source data'],0,'The source difference is still 4. Truncated bar lengths distort the magnitude comparison.'],
 ['UX and tools','What is the strongest basis for choosing a visualisation tool?',['The newest brand name','Fit to the actual task, data, users, integration, cost and governance requirements','A universal 5/5 score','The number of animations'],1,'Tool effectiveness depends on context, including scale, access, maintenance and user capability.'],
 ['Chart interpretation','What is the best first response to an unusual high value?',['Delete it immediately','Assume fraud','Investigate its source and context before deciding how to report it','Hide it with a filter and do not disclose it'],2,'An outlier can be an error or a real event. Keep an audit trail and disclose justified treatment.'],
 ['Chart interpretation','A branch has 90 successes from 100 cases; another has 1 from 10. What is the combined rate?',['50%','100%','91%','About 82.73%'],3,'Combine successes and cases: (90+1)/(100+10) ×100 =82.73%. A simple mean of unequal-group percentages is incorrect here.'],
 ['Prediction and mining','Forecasts are 500, 520, 540, 510; actuals are 510, 515, 430, 505. What is mean absolute error?',['32.5 units','27.5 units','130 units','110 units'],0,'Absolute errors are 10, 5, 110, 5. Their total is 130, divided by 4 forecasts gives32.5 units. The signed mean is 27.5 and can hide cancellation.'],
 ['Prediction and mining','Observed temperatures range from 20°C to 26°C. Estimating sales at 28°C is what?',['Interpolation','Extrapolation','Deduplication','Verification'],1,'28°C is outside the observed range. State that the relationship is being extended beyond the evidence.'],
 ['Big data and OLAP','What does ETL stand for, in order?',['Enter, Test, Link','Extract, Transfer, List','Extract, Transform, Load','Evaluate, Transform, Lock'],2,'Extract retrieves authorised source data; Transform prepares it; Load places it into the intended analytical store.'],
 ['Security and storage','Why might synchronisation alone fail as a recovery strategy?',['It never copies files','It always requires a USB','It proves every file is accurate','Deletion or corruption may propagate to synchronised copies'],3,'Keep suitable separate recoverable versions and test restoration. An aligned current copy is not necessarily a recoverable earlier state.'],
 ['Social behaviour','A post receives 1,000 likes. Which conclusion is supported directly?',['It received 1,000 recorded like actions under the platform measurement','1,000 different people purchased the product','Every customer liked the product','The campaign caused higher profit'],0,'The record measures a platform action. Unique people, sentiment, purchases and profit require further evidence and definitions.'],
 ['Privacy and governance','A student credits the source of a protected chart. What follows?',['The credit always grants permission','Attribution is useful, but reuse still needs a suitable licence, permission or applicable exception','Copyright no longer applies','The entire dataset becomes public domain'],1,'Attribution and authorisation are separate. Check what reuse is permitted and follow the relevant conditions.']
 ];
