 const cards=[
 ['Visual purpose','What are three purposes of visualisation?','Simplify understanding, tell an evidenced story and highlight important results. Select the form for the audience and decision.'],
 ['UX','Distinguish UI and UX.','UI is the controls and presentation a person interacts with. UX is the overall experience of understanding and completing their task.'],
 ['UX','Name the booklet’s four UX factors.','Relevance, audience interpretation, customisation and live analysis. Explain a concrete feature and effect for each.'],
 ['UX','Give a measurable UX criterion.','A representative user identifies the highest late-delivery rate correctly within30 seconds, with the correct filter state and denominator.'],
 ['Errors and bias','Error versus uncertainty versus bias?','An error is a mistake; uncertainty is incomplete knowledge or precision; bias is systematic distortion. Several can occur together.'],
 ['Errors and bias','What is selective reporting bias?','Selecting evidence, such as only profitable months, in a way that systematically distorts the relevant full picture.'],
 ['Blockchain','What does a blockchain preserve, and what does it not prove?','It can support a shared tamper-evident history. It does not by itself prove that every physical-world input was truthful.'],
 ['Security','Authentication versus authorisation?','Authentication checks identity. Authorisation determines permitted access or actions for that identity.'],
 ['Security','Why are backups different from synchronisation?','Backups retain recoverable states. Synchronisation aligns copies and may propagate deletion or corruption. Test restoration.'],
 ['Privacy','Why is a checkbox insufficient by itself?','Meaningful consent also needs an informed, voluntary, current and specific choice by someone with capacity.'],
 ['Big data','Explain the three Vs.','Volume: amount. Variety: forms and structures. Velocity: arrival and processing rate. One case may involve all three.'],
 ['Big data','Storage versus memory?','Storage retains records for later use. Memory holds data and instructions currently being worked on.'],
 ['Warehousing','Explain ETL using a store example.','Extract sales logs, transform product IDs/units and investigate duplicates, then load the prepared records into the analytical store.'],
 ['OLAP','Measure versus dimension?','A measure is a quantity such as revenue. A dimension organises it, such as product, region or month.'],
 ['OLAP','Drill down versus roll up?','Drill down increases detail, such as quarter to month. Roll up summarises at a higher level, such as month to quarter.'],
 ['Prediction','Statistical modelling and machine learning: separate or overlapping?','They overlap. Both can fit relationships and predict. Explain the model, data, assumptions and evaluation rather than treating the labels as exclusive.'],
 ['Prediction','What is overfitting?','Fitting peculiarities of training examples so the model performs poorly on relevant new cases. Check performance on appropriate unseen data.'],
 ['Prediction','How do you calculate mean absolute error?','Take the absolute difference between each forecast and actual, sum those magnitudes and divide by the number of evaluated pairs. Keep the outcome’s units.'],
 ['Privacy','Privacy Act, APPs and OAIC?','The Privacy Act1988(Cth) is the law; APPs are 13 principles for covered entities; OAIC is the federal privacy regulator.'],
 ['Governance','Why keep metadata?','Source, date, purpose, units, field definitions, coverage, transformations and permissions let others interpret and evaluate data.'],
 ['Social behaviour','A data swamp versus a useful data store?','A swamp lacks usable organisation, metadata, quality and governance. More storage alone does not fix it.'],
 ['Interpretation','Aggregation versus filtering?','Aggregation combines records into summaries. Filtering selects a subset of records; it can change the population and denominator.'],
 ['Interpretation','What should happen to a genuine unusual event?','Retain and explain it. If a sensitivity summary excludes it, disclose that choice and show the relevant comparison. Correct verified errors with a record of the change.'],
 ['Design','How do scope and depth differ?','Scope is breadth across data areas; depth is the level of detail. An overview with filters and drill-down can support both.']
 ];
